1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,920
ADAPTED FROM THE ORIGINAL WEB NOVEL
<i>THE EARLY SPRING</i>, BY GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,840
Where were you?

4
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,600
I went to make a call.

5
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,880
Sun Yu.

6
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,600
Wake up.

7
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:52,400
One more round!

8
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,240
One more?

9
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,960
Where's Yao Bei?

10
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,920
She said she wanted to head back
to pack her luggage.

11
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:01,920
Then, she left.

12
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,200
Right.

13
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,240
She got promoted.

14
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,120
She's going to Hong Kong, China.

15
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:09,880
- Promoted?
- She's leaving Beijing.

16
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,600
I almost forgot to tell you this.

17
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,680
I got promoted too.

18
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:18,040
Don't tell me you're leaving Beijing too.

19
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,360
No.

20
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,600
No way.

21
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,640
I'm not leaving until I get
a three-bedroom, one-living-room flat

22
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:23,600
in Beijing.

23
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,800
Don't leave.

24
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:28,360
- No.
- None of you can leave Beijing.

25
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,680
If you leave, no one will keep me company.

26
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,120
Don't worry.

27
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,400
I won't leave. I'll grow old with you.

28
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,440
Pinky promise. None of you can leave.

29
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:41,120
We'll stay in Beijing
and make our dreams come true.

30
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,840
Make our dreams come true together.

31
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,360
Don't go.

32
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:49,680
Yes.

33
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,800
Already passing out?

34
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:53,880
Come on. You guys are boring.

35
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,600
I'm just getting started,
and you guys are out cold.

36
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:58,840
Lumi.

37
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:00,840
Do you have a boyfriend?

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,000
So many of them.

39
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,040
I'm sure you can have more.

40
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,520
We have a blind date event tomorrow.

41
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,440
Come check it out.

42
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:09,040
You can get any guy you want.

43
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,080
I want one who looks like Eddie Peng.

44
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,520
Eddie Peng?

45
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,400
You might have encountered
a pig-butchering scam.

46
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,720
You don't have a guy like that?

47
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,960
Why bother mentioning it then?

48
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:23,440
BEING WITH YOU IS LIKE A LEAP OF FAITH

49
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,200
Morning.

50
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,520
Morning, Tao.

51
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,440
Morning.

52
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:33,920
You're so early today.

53
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,800
- Morning.
- Morning, Lumi.

54
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:42,600
You're back in full force.

55
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,240
You even put on red lipstick.

56
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,520
We partied until so late last night,

57
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,040
I almost couldn't wake up this morning.

58
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,920
I agreed to be there for Sun Yu's event,

59
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,280
so I dressed up a bit.

60
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,560
Oh, the girl with the red sweater?
The matchmaker?

61
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:57,480
Yes.

62
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:00,320
Don't go to her matchmaking event.

63
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,160
Why not meet up
with my childhood friend first?

64
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,720
I'm just there to show support,
not for the blind date.

65
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,680
When you're there this evening,

66
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:08,840
check out the guys for me.

67
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,480
See if there's someone like Eddie Peng,

68
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,400
like what your friend said.

69
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,520
If you find one, keep him for me.

70
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,440
Sure.

71
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:19,959
- Morning, Mr. Luan.
- Boss.

72
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,920
Morning, Luke.

73
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,640
Luan Nian.

74
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,680
I want to hold onto you.

75
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,920
LUKE: LUMI, COME TO MY OFFICE

76
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,040
Come in.

77
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,720
Boss. How can I help?

78
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:11,560
How is the progress of the proposal
that you and Shang Zhitao are working on?

79
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,760
I told her to submit it tomorrow.

80
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,720
She has a blind date today.

81
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,920
A blind date?

82
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,080
Yes. She can't work overtime
every day, can she?

83
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:23,080
We must all live our lives. Right, boss?

84
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,000
Do you know why you work overtime?

85
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,480
Because you don't focus on work
during office hours.

86
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,040
I need the proposal today.

87
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,000
Luke.

88
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,400
Come with me.

89
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:02,040
My work is done.

90
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,200
Overtime.

91
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,320
You want the proposal?

92
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,760
I already sent it to Lumi.

93
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:09,200
There is something else. Come.

94
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,520
The seat belt is stuck.

95
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:55,800
Thank you.

96
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:57,520
Have you gotten the driving license?

97
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,280
I got it last month.

98
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,520
I'll take you to practice driving.

99
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,840
You will participate in Yueteng's
new car test drive event.

100
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:16,640
So by working overtime,
you mean I need to practice my driving?

101
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,240
I mean I'm working overtime
to practice with you.

102
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,000
<i>Sorry, I can't be there.</i>

103
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,840
<i>Emergency overtime.</i>

104
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:58,320
Take the wheel. I'll sit next to you.

105
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,600
Practice with your car?

106
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,960
Don't you have a driving license?

107
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,360
Pull your seat forward.

108
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,600
Practice.

109
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,440
Go now.

110
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,200
You were so eager to leave work today.

111
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,800
Who were you planning to see?

112
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,280
My flatmate.

113
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,800
You have a blind date with your flatmate?

114
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,920
Just how did you get your driving license?

115
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,720
Let me go out and check.

116
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:24,680
No need.

117
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,760
I'll drive.

118
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,360
Sorry.

119
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:54,200
You haven't answered me.

120
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,120
Who do you have a blind date with?

121
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,760
Are…

122
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,640
Are you jealous?

123
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,480
You wish.

124
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:15,120
My flatmate

125
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:17,960
works in the marketing division
of a dating website.

126
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,160
So I--

127
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,480
<i>It was an accident.</i>

128
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,680
<i>You had an accident, I know.</i>

129
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:21,040
<i>But what about Luan Nian?</i>

130
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,520
<i>Was he also an accident?</i>

131
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,400
<i>First, he saved you,</i>

132
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:27,160
<i>then, he created the happy accident.</i>

133
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:34,040
The way I see it,
he has been playing the long game.

134
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,600
<i>Date a few people.</i>

135
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:38,240
Experiment a bit while you're young.

136
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,240
<i>We only live for around 30,000 days.</i>

137
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,600
<i>If you like someone, tell them.</i>

138
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:47,200
<i>If you miss them, go see them.</i>

139
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,360
As long as we're safe
and it's what we want,

140
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,680
we have nothing to lose.

141
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:30,800
If you want,

142
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,440
we can keep our relationship private.

143
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:46,800
You…

144
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,120
You don't wear pajamas?

145
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,880
You're wearing mine.

146
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,280
I'll return them to you later.

147
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,360
I want them now.

148
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,040
I have to go home.

149
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,520
I have work tomorrow.

150
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,200
Sure.

151
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,800
Let me call Mr. Liu. He'll drive you home.

152
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,200
- Don't.
- Mr. Liu.

153
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,360
Sorry for calling you this late.

154
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,840
Can you send someone home for me?

155
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:30,080
Yes, she's at my home.

156
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,160
What?

157
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,120
I don't want him to drive me back.

158
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:50,080
He'll recognize me.

159
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,240
So, what do you want?

160
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:59,000
I'll sleep in the guest room.

161
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,160
Planning to disappear tomorrow
without saying goodbye

162
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:04,880
and just leave me a small note?

163
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,320
I won't leave you a note this time.

164
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,840
Last time, it was an accident.

165
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,760
But this time, it's not.

166
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,960
What is it then?

167
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:26,360
I don't want to lose my job.

168
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:29,320
I don't want to jeopardize my job either.

169
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,800
I don't want others to think
I'm taking shortcuts

170
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,400
by relying on you.

171
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:51,160
I'll sleep in the guest room.

172
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:50,920
You're making it more obvious.

173
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:53,440
Can you

174
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,360
drop me off at the subway?

175
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:00,640
Eat first.

176
00:17:14,359 --> 00:17:16,599
You made this yourself?

177
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:17,880
It's delicious.

178
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,040
Can I have one more glass?

179
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:43,600
Yes.

180
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:44,640
Thank you.

181
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:28,320
Just drop me off
at the subway entrance in front.

182
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:32,280
JINTAI XIZHAO SUBWAY STATION

183
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:36,760
We missed it.

184
00:18:37,920 --> 00:18:39,640
It's pouring. No need for the hassle.

185
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,200
No one's around at this time.

186
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,600
Just go up first.

187
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,680
SHANG ZHITAO

188
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:35,000
<i>Floor One.</i>

189
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,280
Coming up from the parking lot?

190
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:38,560
Did you buy a car?

191
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:39,640
No.

192
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,320
Sun Yu gave me a ride.

193
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,080
Your friend is so much better
than my boyfriend.

194
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,480
It's raining,
and my car is restricted today,

195
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,000
and he didn't even offer
to give me a ride.

196
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:51,960
Doesn't your boyfriend always pick you up?

197
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,520
He's quite considerate.

198
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,640
What's the point of having a boyfriend
if he's not considerate?

199
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,880
I have to deal with a mean boss
with a weird temper

200
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:59,560
at work already.

201
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,080
Dealing with another one after work

202
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:03,240
will make my life miserable.

203
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:08,400
Where were you last night?

204
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,760
You didn't even change your clothes.

205
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:15,680
You're making it so obvious.

206
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,480
It's not even a big deal. Just show it.

207
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:22,160
Linda from Sales
always shows off her sexcapades.

208
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,280
- Boss.
- Morning, Luke.

209
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,960
Sun Yu is that good, huh?

210
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:53,280
Was he as amazing as she said he was?

211
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,680
Introduce him to me.

212
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,640
- I'll gauge him for you.
- Enough…

213
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:58,400
Stop guessing.

214
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,680
My laptop is…

215
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,440
What's wrong with your laptop?

216
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:05,240
I left my laptop in Sun Yu's car.

217
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,680
I need to call her
and ask her to bring it back.

218
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,920
I'll go to Luke then.

219
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,320
What for?

220
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:14,480
I'll tell him
you didn't go home last night.

221
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:17,120
Don't. What are you telling him?

222
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,840
Why are you so scared?

223
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,840
Are you traumatized by him or what?

224
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,200
We'll be talking about the proposal.

225
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,760
He couldn't care less
about the man you saw.

226
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:29,280
Shouldn't you check with Alex
first about the proposal?

227
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,560
Yikes.

228
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,120
Thank you for the reminder.

229
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,760
Otherwise, I would've been scolded.

230
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:36,080
Alex comes in late.

231
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,160
I'll get a cup of coffee.

232
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:38,480
Do you want anything?

233
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,560
No, thanks. Go. I'll make the call.

234
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,840
Brandish it.

235
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:53,680
Luke.

236
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:56,120
I left my laptop bag in your car.

237
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:58,520
<i>I'll bring it to you later.</i>

238
00:21:59,040 --> 00:21:59,880
No need.

239
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,520
I'm at the parking lot.

240
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:03,520
I'll find an empty place and wait for you.

241
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,320
<i>Parking lot emergency exit.</i>

242
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,560
<i>I'm there.</i>

243
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:21,640
<i>When you come in, stomp your feet twice.</i>

244
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:55,960
Even an arms smuggler
isn't as cautious as you.

245
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,160
Thank you.

246
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,080
What are you afraid of?

247
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:21,880
I don't want people to see us.

248
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:24,640
We must maintain a distance at work.

249
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:28,440
And you maintain the distance
by inviting me

250
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:30,400
to a dark staircase?

251
00:25:06,600 --> 00:25:07,520
<i>Shang Zhitao.</i>

252
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:11,600
<i>Let's date in secret.</i>

253
00:25:20,800 --> 00:25:21,640
<i>Okay.</i>

254
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,920
<i>But you can't tell anyone about us.</i>

255
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:38,400
<i>Including your friends,</i>

256
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,040
<i>your family…</i>

257
00:25:44,280 --> 00:25:45,200
<i>and your colleagues.</i>

258
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,120
<i>Especially at the office.</i>

259
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:52,960
<i>You are my superior,</i>
<i>and I am your subordinate.</i>

260
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,640
<i>Fine with me.</i>

261
00:26:10,280 --> 00:26:12,240
<i>We'll remain exclusive to each other.</i>

262
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:15,040
<i>I'll come see you every Friday.</i>

263
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:19,080
<i>Okay. It's Friday today.</i>

264
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,080
- <i>See you in a bit.</i>
- <i>See you in a bit.</i>

265
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:52,800
THIRD FLOOR

266
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:11,920
Hi, Mr. Luan.

267
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:12,880
Hi, Mr. Luan.

268
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,120
<i>During my second year in Lime,</i>

269
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:32,600
<i>he and I started dating in secret.</i>

270
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:40,800
